  3.601553881090431*^9},ExpressionUUID->"b353c7ae-f8a0-448f-9250-\
2affc6c4b0f1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Note stars have fixed equator coordinates \[Dash] that is they don't change \
with time. (Actually they do change a little with time due to the precession \
of the ",
 StyleBox["Earth",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "'s axis, but the effect is very small. Use the ",
 StyleBox["Epoch",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " option to see the effect.)"
}], "Text",
 ImageRegion->{{0, 1}, {0, 
  1}},ExpressionUUID->"07eb0b07-7598-4bdc-949e-082d6a589c49"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The brightest 25 stars have also been given aliases, so for examples you \
can use ",
 StyleBox["Sirius",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Canopus",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Polaris",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " etc as star names."
}], "Text",
 ImageRegion->{{0, 1}, {0, 
  1}},ExpressionUUID->"db959de5-5cbe-4841-915b-714720f0fed0"],

Cell["\<\
You can also find the equator coordinates of a point relative to the horizon \
at some local time. For example:\
\>", "Text",
 ImageRegion->{{0, 1}, {0, 
  1}},ExpressionUUID->"604c9d6c-55ec-4556-91d2-f6a0a7f6502f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"EquatorCoordinates", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Azimuth", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"60", " ", "\[Degree]"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"Altitude", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"30", " ", "\[Degree]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1993", ",", "11", ",", "17", ",", "3", ",", "20", ",", "0"}], 
    "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8a8a2480-332e-404d-b8cb-\
59ec346207a6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Ascension", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"8.958837356708955`", " ", "Hour"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"Declination", "\[Rule]", "0.0357012135015096`"}]}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.6015539147552905`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4eed1587-75c1-4603-b5e6-\
d62904897a82"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["7.1.4. Horizon Coordinates command",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "\nThese are useful when you are out in the field. A negative ",
 StyleBox["Altitude",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " would mean the object is currently below the horizon."
}], "Text",
 ImageRegion->{{0, 1}, {0, 
  1}},ExpressionUUID->"1ac120e9-bdcd-45b8-a5e1-33080919d1c2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Information", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<HorizonCoordinates\>\"", ",", 
   RowBox[{"LongForm", "\[Rule]", "False"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 ImageRegion->{{0, 1}, {0, 
  1}},ExpressionUUID->"6ffa1b45-1ba9-4abe-a24d-b09427de2285"],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox["\<\"HorizonCoordinates[object, date] returns the Azimuth, Altitude \
and Distance of the object (a planet or a star) on the given date. An example \
planet would be Mars, and an example star would be Alpha.Centaurus. \
HorizonCoordinates[equatorcoords, date] will convert the equatorcoords into \
horizoncoords for the current location. An example equatorcoords would be \
{Ascension->18*Hour, Declination->30*Degree}. If date is omitted the current \
Date[] is used.\"\>", "MSG"]], "Print", "PrintUsage",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.60155395420776*^9},
 CellTags->
  "Info3601557554-3591912",ExpressionUUID->"893577cf-d8f9-42ac-ae07-\
4f49a20af4ff"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["HorizonCoordinates",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " command can be applied to objects like ",
 StyleBox["Mars",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Moon",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Io",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (solar system objects), ",
 StyleBox["Sirius",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Alpha.Centaurus",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (stars), ",
 StyleBox["Leo",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["UrsaMajor",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (constellations), ",
 StyleBox["SouthCelestialPole",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Zenith",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (special objects) etc."
}], "Text",
 ImageRegion->{{0, 1}, {0, 
  1}},ExpressionUUID->"ebc61e75-9030-4e4a-9371-43c839174a8a"],

Cell["Here are some basic examples:", "Text",
 ImageRegion->{{0, 1}, {0, 
  1}},ExpressionUUID->"124c0c4c-1e02-4644-b404-e6b538da6745"],

